{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e","id":1234466,"title":"Don't Understand the Calculation for the Inheritance Background (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-12T18:00:36-07:00","id":1234466,"title":"Don't Understand the Calculation for the Inheritance Background (2E)","content":"OK,<br /> So first, pardon me: I only have access to the Background as it's explained in MoEP: Infernals, which only gives the Background a brief treatment. As near as I understand it (and searching on here keeps getting me the Permanent Essence Scores of both parents added together and divided by two), I must be missing something.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, every Half-Caste whose Exalted parent has an Essence 5, who has a divine or Demon parent with an Essence of 5 would be Inheritance 5...and it doesn't seem to make sense if nearly every Half-Caste God/Demon-Blooded is Inheritance 4-5. Have I missed a step in the equation which determines their Inheritance rating?<br /> <br /> Apologies if this is an archaic question/issue, but I mainly approach Exalted from a fan-fiction writing standpoint, but I try to maintain at least moderate mechanical fidelity. Moving over to 3E isn't something I can afford as yet, so here I am.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T21:08:07-07:00","id":1234525,"title":"","content":"The key is that Essence 5 is not particularly common. Mortals have an Essence of 1, a starting 2e Exalt usually has an Essence of 2, most 2e First Circle Demons/Terrestrial Gods/Elementals have an Essence of 2 or 3. So most God-Blooded are Inheritance 1 (Essence 1 mortal with Essence 2 demon/god/elemental, (1+2)/2 = 1.5, round down to 1).<br /> <br /> Cases of powerful Exalts mating with Second-or-Third Circle Demons/Celestial Gods/Elemental Dragons are rare; there are going to be only a handful of God-Blooded of such powerful lineage, and thus Inheritance 4 or 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T00:08:43-07:00","id":1234552,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're drastically overestimating the number of E5+ beings in the setting; most Dragon-Blooded don't even get to Essence 3 in their lifetimes, IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T03:05:43-07:00","id":1234568,"title":"","content":"The thing to remember about Inheritance is that its generational.<br /> Its pretty easy for an Exalt with similar means to a PC to have kids with Inheritance 4-5, but the grandchildren will probably have a lower rating unless they find partners of a similar supernatural lineage or start in-breeding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:49:23-07:00","id":1234747,"title":"","content":"In our game, the Solar and Lunar had an Inheritance 3 baby; that's the child of two Exalts.<br /> The &quot;average&quot; demon-blood is likely Inheritance 1 or 2; even the half-demon child of a second-circle demon probably has a mortal parent, so even if their mum is Essence 6, but their dad is Essence 1, that's Inheritance 3.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could have the child of an Exalt and a second-circle demon or elemental dragon, but how many Lunar elders, Sidereal elders or Dragon-blood elders have kids with second-circle demons, high-ranked gods or elemental dragons?<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's a handful of Inheritance 4-5 half-divine star-children, and a few half-Infernal demon-blood babies, but it's certainly not average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-13-2018, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:05:28-07:00","id":1234753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234747#post1234747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our game, the Solar and Lunar had an Inheritance 3 baby; that's the child of two Exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that house-ruled? Because Exalts don't normally start having x blooded children until essence 4.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:55:29-07:00","id":1234765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234753#post1234753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that house-ruled? Because Exalts don't normally start having x blooded children until essence 4.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There were allowances for living in a powerful Demesne or having a high Cult rating to lower the required Essence rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T13:56:47-07:00","id":1234766,"title":"","content":"The Solar had Essence 3, the Lunar Essence 4.<br /> (I think you round down, I might be remembering wrong. I'm also not sure if it's a half-Solar or half-Lunar. I can't remember if higher essence or being a Solar trumps. But he's 1 so there's no way to tell. And the edition has changed.)<br /> <br /> Well, by the time he was born, the Solar father was Essence 4, but that's a bit late.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 07-13-2018, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:09:45-07:00","id":1234770,"title":"","content":"Thanks all,<br /> I *thought* that the logistics of dual-supernatural-lineage was what I was missing, but I wanted to be sure. No, I didn't believe two Essence 5 beings having kids was common, but the Inheritance rating is the same whatever the parents' Essence scores are if they both match. So, an Essence 3 Exalt and an Essence 3 God, leads to Inheritance 3 offspring. That seemed like it might be more powerful than intended, but again a) I realize from reading here prior to getting registered that the general consensus is the Inheritance mechanism isn't particularly well-loved, and b) My own personal experience with it comes from the truncated explanation it gets in MoEP: Infernals.<br /> <br /> I truly appreciate everyone being willing to wade in and clarify the matter for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:10:09-07:00","id":1234771,"title":"","content":"I doubt there'll be much of a numbers game in 3e but a few rough guidelines would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:59:42-07:00","id":1234793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wyldwraith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234770#post1234770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks all,<br /> I *thought* that the logistics of dual-supernatural-lineage was what I was missing, but I wanted to be sure. No, I didn't believe two Essence 5 beings having kids was common, but the Inheritance rating is the same whatever the parents' Essence scores are if they both match. So, an Essence 3 Exalt and an Essence 3 God, leads to Inheritance 3 offspring. That seemed like it might be more powerful than intended, but again a) I realize from reading here prior to getting registered that the general consensus is the Inheritance mechanism isn't particularly well-loved, and b) My own personal experience with it comes from the truncated explanation it gets in MoEP: Infernals.<br /> <br /> I truly appreciate everyone being willing to wade in and clarify the matter for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As most people have already pointed out, the imense majority of the god-blooded everywhere will have only one supernatural parent. But yeah, the way the system handled it back then, even a spirit + mortal sorcerer/supernatural martial artist coupling would have something of a nice leg-up in passing supernatural puisance to their children. I have of late toyed with making an updated take of Inheritance and the multiple god-blooded through artifact &amp; evocation mechanics and the results have been entertaining overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T16:41:39-07:00","id":1234820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234766#post1234766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you round down</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah so you do.<br /> I'd assumed one rounded up and hadn't checked the rules for calculating Inheritance in a while because I think it's a pretty shitty execution in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T20:05:54-07:00","id":1234856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234820#post1234820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah so you do.<br /> I'd assumed one rounded up and hadn't checked the rules for calculating Inheritance in a while because I think it's a pretty shitty execution in general.</div> </div> </div> </div> Half the supernatural parent''s Essence rounded down for Inheritance ain't bad - as long as you keep legacies separate, much like two level 2 artifacts do not an artifact level 4 make, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T03:48:14-07:00","id":1234902,"title":"","content":"It is bad. A problem with Inheritance was that for a god blooded game you needed to standardise the power of the the PC's parents, the fact that you round down makes it even worse because it means the child of Erembour (essence 9) and the child of Ligier (essence 10) aren't supposed to play in the same sandbox.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T06:32:29-07:00","id":1234928,"title":"","content":"What you could do is instead of dividing the parent's essences by two, you roll that many dice. <br /> <br /> So <i>on average</i> it winds up being the same but there's more wiggle room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:34:13-07:00","id":1234947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234928#post1234928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you could do is instead of dividing the parent's essences by two, you roll that many dice.<br /> <br /> So <i>on average</i> it winds up being the same but there's more wiggle room.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... sort of even worse. So instead of assigning dots to players based on her preference for the power level of her chronicle, the Storyteller is supposed to trust everything to dice rolls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:01:01-07:00","id":1234975,"title":"","content":"No, I was joking.<br /> <br /> I knew I should have given some indication of that in the post.<br /> <br /> Having the range be sort of based on that could work though. &quot;Anywhere between diddly squat and twice your parent's essences. average is about half.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:35:32-07:00","id":1234986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234902#post1234902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is bad. A problem with Inheritance was that for a god blooded game you needed to standardise the power of the the PC's parents, the fact that you round down makes it even worse because it means the child of Erembour (essence 9) and the child of Ligier (essence 10) aren't supposed to play in the same sandbox.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ligier x Erembour case could be solved, under the same mechanics, by giving the mortal parent having one more Essence dot.<br /> Mortals could have Essence 1-3 in previous editions, remember? Wiggle room existed in those sandboxes.<br /> If it was bad indeed the real reason was, imho, because Inheritance, like Liege and other badly though backgrounds, gave freebies points in the first place, most certainly not a thing to do with the backgrounds format.Mathematics were icingg in the messy cake once you start meta-minmaxing stuff like that. <br /> <br /> Really hoping they do something quite different, like using something like the evocation system, to portray god-blood supernatural legacy this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:59:50-07:00","id":1234990,"title":"","content":"There is something else about this I was mulling over,<br /> Realistically, people tend to have children (when it's intentional) with people they can respect. Not insects they could literally kill with an idle thought. That, shared perspectives, ability to relate to one's partner's life experience...and not being terrified out of your mind all the time that your powerful enemies are going to squish your mortal love interest to strike at you.<br /> <br /> In other words, I actually think that in many cases, both parents often WILL be supernatural. Sure, there will be gobs of cases where that isn't the case, but many Exalts likely try to keep some emotional distance between themselves and mortals they find themselves attracted to. It hurts too much to bury someone after only the tiniest fraction of your own life has gone by. Now, that isn't to say that means these childrens' parents will be powerhouses...but I imagine that -blooded of various types often get together with other Ghost/Fae/Demon/God-Blooded. That Outcaste DBs might find love for a time with a small god (or a more powerful Terrestrial god, even).<br /> <br /> Yes, there are all the cases where the supernatural partner simply finds a way to make their mortal love interest live longer (like Fakharu, the Western Censor). Yet I could definitely see significant numbers of those with a supernatural heritage finding common ground, friendship, and later love with others of similar heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T11:41:34-07:00","id":1235029,"title":"","content":"Hence a lot of godblooded being a product of one night stands, I guess.<br /> <br /> Sometimes a god just goes &quot;I'mma tap that&quot;.<br /> <br /> But also a lot of them have a somewhat healthier view of mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T13:56:31-07:00","id":1235077,"title":"","content":"Equal matings between the powerful are not going to be the origin of a large percentage of the God-Blooded, because there are simply not enough of the powerful for them to make up a large percentage. There's less than a thousand Celestial Exalts, and Terrestrials are in the tens of thousands. But there are hundreds of millions of mortals. And there are lots and lots of Essence 2 Terrestial gods and elementals in Creation, while mighty ones tend to wind up in Yu Shan. The vast majority of cases of humans conceiving a child with a spirit in-setting are going to be mortal with Essence 2 spirit, because the vast majority of contacts between humans of any kind and spirits of any kind are going to be mortal with Essence 2 spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T00:05:07-07:00","id":1235468,"title":"","content":"Well yes,<br /> Just going by the over-scale of looking at the total population, you're absolutely right Verzio. I was simply saying that OUT OF the various God/Fae/Ghost/Demon-Blooded who exist, all the various Terrestrial Gods, Elementals, and Celestial Gods slumming it (Burning Feather, Goddess of Intoxication, seems to have a bunch of canon God-Blooded descendants, for example)...It won't be uncommon for two individuals with shared supernatural heritage to choose to pair off.<br /> <br /> Given the numbers, their offspring will of course be vastly outnumbered by a) regular mortals, and b) Single supernatural parent -Blooded. (Except perhaps Demon-Blooded, given the sheer proliferation of 1st-Circle Demons escaping into Creation. The escape-conditions of the various 1st Circle Demons are things common enough to happen fairly often given Creation's size.) I was more saying that the factors I described mean there are compelling reasons for supernaturals to pair with other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Especially when you talk about the -Blooded getting with a member of their &quot;source species.&quot; While many mortals might fear/hate a Fae-Blooded, a Raksha certainly wouldn't hold the Fae-Blooded's heritage against them. Similarly, a Ghost-Blooded raised in a Shadowland might think nothing of having a Ghostly lover who possesses some comely mortal. Many Demons might find the demonic mutations some Demon-Bloods possess that Demon-Blood's most attractive features given the difference in Demonic aesthetic sense. Same for a Lesser Elemental Dragon looking at a God-Blood who descends from an Elemental of their element.<br /> <br /> In the scope of Creation's Total Population, such beings will always be a vast minority. It had simply occurred to me there are good reasons why a supernatural looking to start a family might not want to do so with a regular mortal. Particularly if that supernatural has already experienced one or more of the drawbacks of pairing with a normal human being in a prior relationship. A Faeblooded who was happily living with their mortal spouse, until some people from the neighboring village who'd lost loved ones to the Fair Folk learned of the Faeblood who was living in a secluded cabin in the woods, came to kill said Faeblood by burning down the cabin in the middle of the night, and ended up killing their human lover instead.<br /> <br /> To say nothing of the ambitious. A God who had God-blooded offspring as part of a plan to increase their worship in Creation might think nothing of taking their plan a step further, arrange for a Supernatural who owes them to be willing to get with their God-Blooded son or daughter, and tell said son or daughter &quot;If you're hoping to become a God/Goddess yourself one day, get with the program.&quot; For more sinister reasons (or maybe not, depending on the God)...I could DEFINITELY see a 2nd-Circle Demon like Sondok simply demand one of their children procreate with a Demon or pay the price for their defiance.<br /> <br /> All of these circumstances are only contributing to a small minority of the total population, but there's no reason to believe they don't exist. Tiny minority or not, the individuals who result from such unions can definitely have a massive impact on Creation wildly disproportionate to their numbers. The God-Blooded son of the Volcano God Hamoji is the premier Captain, who'd be the go-to if the Feathered One needed an Admiral during hostilities on behalf of Wavecrest. If the ensuing war with Coral aroused Siakal enough she wanted to get with him, their son or daughter could become the West's non-Exalt champion against the Lintha or Silver Prince.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T03:15:52-07:00","id":1235488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1234986#post1234986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> If it was bad indeed the real reason was, imho, because Inheritance, like Liege and other badly though backgrounds, gave freebies points in the first place, most certainly not a thing to do with the backgrounds format.Mathematics were icing in the messy cake once you start meta-minmaxing stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Really hoping they do something quite different, like using something like the evocation system, to portray god-blood supernatural legacy this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the whole bonus point set-up is horrible and the 1-5 scale takes an already limited thing like a god blooded game and makes it even more limited.<br /> I'm just annoyed at finding another thing wrong with it that I'd missed for years.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T10:07:50-07:00","id":1235606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234466-don-t-understand-the-calculation-for-the-inheritance-background-2e?p=1235488#post1235488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the whole bonus point set-up is horrible and the 1-5 scale takes an already limited thing like a god blooded game and makes it even more limited.<br /> I'm just annoyed at finding another thing wrong with it that I'd missed for years.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Too true. Makes me remember those ridiculously arbitrary and bizantine ghoul mechanics for Masquerade. Now that is an utterly useless thing some people just can't leave alone in limbo and forget...<br /> <br /> Me, i decided to retooling Inheritance using 3e Artifact &amp; Evocation mechanics, just to see how could it turn out, nothing to fancy.<br /> - Inheritance 1-2, just some minor benefit, like whatt one might get from a mutation, thaumaturgy ritual or equivalent low-level supernatural merit.<br /> - Inheritance 3-5, that opens the room not only to awakening one's Essence, but with it the potential to develop a set of evocation-esque powers reflecting springing from the interplay of divine legacy and a hero's own temperament and budding personal legend.<br /> <br /> The results have been quite fun so far - one player even invested in having multiple Inheritance, due to a very, very messy family history of spirit deallings and it has worked pretty well so far, to the point that we have considered taking things a little further by mining other Artifact related mechanics for inane stuff like &quot;refining the divinity&quot; within one's veins, sharing legacies through magical vows and a bbunch of other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T11:09:55-07:00","id":1235641,"title":"","content":"Just for the record,<br /> I wholeheartedly agree that Bonus Points was *not* the ideal way to go about this Background. Even if I were to go in a similar direction, I would've done something like X # of starting Spirit Charms, Y # of Parent-Derived capacities (like becoming Immaterial, for those with the highest of Inheritances). Just a pool of bonus points doesn't really make sense. I get that the points were intended to represent that at-creation powers such a being possesses...but not being more explicit wasn't helpful in focusing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}